<!--
  ============================================================================
  BiomeAnimalDanglingRefs_Fix.xml          Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  THE BUG
  =======
  Sibling of AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml. Same engine method, opposite
  failure. BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal() builds a Dictionary keyed on
  PawnKindDef:

      foreach (record in biome.wildAnimals)
          dict.Add(record.animal, record.commonality);

  If a wildAnimals entry names a PawnKindDef that does not exist, the def
  loader logs one quiet "could not resolve cross-reference" line and leaves
  record.animal as NULL. The record itself is NOT removed. Dictionary.Add
  then throws on the null key:

      System.ArgumentNullException: Value cannot be null. Parameter name: key
        at System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2.TryInsert
        at RimWorld.BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal (PawnKindDef animalDef)
        at RimWorld.BiomeDef+<get_AllWildAnimals>d__94.MoveNext ()

  Observed live on this stack, 2026-08-10: this killed Choose Wild Animal
  Spawns in its static constructor, so the MOD WAS DEAD AT STARTUP. It had
  been dead for three consecutive loads, each time behind a different mask:

      load 1 : ArgumentException     duplicate key   (Armadillo, fixed)
      load 2 : ArgumentNullException null BiomeDef   (our own li bug, fixed)
      load 3 : ArgumentNullException null PawnKindDef (THIS, the real one)

  Same exception type and same stack frame across loads 2 and 3, different
  cause. Read what is null, not just where it threw.

  ROOT CAUSE, TRACED  [VERIFIED 2026-08-10]
  =========================================
  Primordial Geysers (IronScruff.PrimordialGeysers, WS 2896731795) ships two
  compatibility patches that inject animals into its own biome:

      1.6/Patches/PrimordialGeysers_AlphaAnimalsPatch.xml
      1.6/Patches/PrimordialGeysers_VanillaAnimalsExpandedPatch.xml

  Both are guarded by PatchOperationFindMod on the MOD NAME only. The mods
  are installed, so the guards pass and the entries are added. But five of
  the named PawnKindDefs do not exist in the versions we load:

    AEXP_Badger, AEXP_Muskox, AEXP_Moose, AEXP_Porcupine
        Vanilla Animals Expanded (WS 2871933948) defines these ONLY in its
        1.6NotOdyssey folder. Its LoadFolders.xml reads:
            <li IfModNotActive="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">1.6NotOdyssey</li>
        Odyssey IS active here, so VAE deliberately drops those four to avoid
        colliding with Odyssey's own badger/muskox/moose/porcupine. Correct
        behaviour by VAE; Primordial Geysers just never accounted for it.

    AA_WaywardMobileAssembler
        Removed from Alpha Animals. Alpha Genes blacklists the name and Alpha
        Animals has its corpse entry commented out in GenomeTable_Alpha.xml.

  This is the "MayRequire / FindMod checks the mod, not the def" trap, but
  with a far worse consequence than the usual harmless unresolved reference.

  DESIGN
  ======
  Remove the five dangling biome-side entries.

  Note this INVERTS the rule stated in AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml ("always
  remove the animal side, never the biome side"). That rule exists so we never
  lose a spawn. It does not apply here: these entries resolve to null, so they
  spawn nothing at all. Removing them costs exactly zero content, and the
  biome already lists vanilla <Porcupine> and <Moose> in its own def anyway.

  Not remapped to the Odyssey equivalents on purpose. Remapping would ADD
  spawns to a biome, which is a design decision, not a crash fix.

  LOAD ORDER  [VERIFIED 2026-08-10]
  =================================
  These nodes do not exist on disk. They are CREATED at runtime by Primordial
  Geysers' patches, so this patch must apply after them. Patches run in mod
  load order:

      Primordial Geysers   entry 252
      Jawa_Patches         entry 562   (LAST of 562 active)

  Moved to last on 2026-08-10, so this holds by construction rather than by
  luck. Keep it last.

  Because the targets are patch-created, validate_patch.py reports 0 on-disk
  matches for every xpath below. That is EXPECTED here and is not a silent
  no-op. The validator sees unpatched defs only.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Every op is wrapped in PatchOperationConditional testing the exact node. If
  Primordial Geysers fixes its patches, or either animal mod restores the
  defs, each op becomes a silent no-op instead of a red error.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
  Expected in Player.log:
    * "No Verse.PawnKindDef named AEXP_Badger found to give to
      RimWorld.BiomeAnimalRecord"   and its four siblings: GONE
    * "Error in static constructor of ChooseWildAnimalSpawns.Main": GONE
    * total unresolved cross-references: 30 to 25
  If CWAS still dies with a null key, another biome has a dangling entry that
  did not log; grep the log for BiomeAnimalRecord and repeat this treatment.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. AA_WaywardMobileAssembler  (removed from Alpha Animals)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AA_WaywardMobileAssembler</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AA_WaywardMobileAssembler</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. AEXP_Badger      (VAE 1.6NotOdyssey only; Odyssey is active)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Badger</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Badger</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       3. AEXP_Muskox      (ditto)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Muskox</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Muskox</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       4. AEXP_Moose       (ditto; biome already lists vanilla Moose)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Moose</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Moose</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       5. AEXP_Porcupine   (ditto; biome already lists vanilla Porcupine)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Porcupine</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers"]/wildAnimals/AEXP_Porcupine</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
